ying they want it  actually know what it is  and part of the confusion i mean even  when you say socialism versus democratic  socialism  the the real question is socialism  versus social democracy democratic  socialism  as traditionally defined is socialism  what i  think you mean is social democracy in  the sort of northern european style  so the first question is going to be  does the word  socialism get completely redefined to  mean social democracy or are people in  your generation  actually clamoring for socializing the  means of production i mean to ask you  which do you mean when you talk about  socialism  that's a great question um i say a lot  of people who watch a lot of  like theory or read a lot of theory like  sort of are okay with the idea of  socializing  lots of industries like more than just  the resource industries that  um uh that venezuela and norway has done  like oils and stuff  but as as far as like uh  how they like express their views  through their voting and express their  views through to  like political candidates and such i  really only see as  a social democracy being like the only  way to express like  far left um thought now at least okay  so that gets directly into part two  which is  if you are an accelerationist then your  belief would be that the path to  socialism however you define it  is a sort of breakdown of the current  system that we have  to be rebuilt directly into socialism  my view is an incrementalist view  because  i believe that when you look at history  that's the way that it has worked  and so no matter what your definition of  socialism is whether it is  as far to the center as social democracy  or as far to the left as you know  marxist leninism or whatever  whatever it may be yeah um the next step  i believe is social democracy either way  so the immediate question is  is the entire left that is at social  democracy and  further left going to unite around  social democracy because i think  we should all recogni